# XSH localtime(), localtime_r()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# TZ is always given in the second form of XBD 8.3 (std offset [dst
# [offset] [,rule]]), with names no TZ database is expected to hold, and a
# rule whenever there is a dst part (without one, the change dates are
# implementation-defined). Every local time checked is non-negative and
# in a year from 1970 on, where XBD 4.19 defines the relationship; the
# test computes the expected UTC instants itself from the rule.

assertion  XSH.localtime.001
anchor     functions/localtime.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap08.html#8.3/TZ
class      required
since      1988
says       With TZ set to a standard time only ("PCT3", "PCE-5:30",
           "PCP+4:15:30"), localtime() returns the broken-down time of
           the value minus the offset (3 h, -5 h 30 min, 4 h 15 min 30 s),
           related to it by the XBD 4.19 expression, with tm_mon, tm_mday
           and tm_wday matching, and tm_isdst 0.
test       t/001-std-offset.c

assertion  XSH.localtime.002
anchor     functions/localtime.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap08.html#8.3/TZ
class      required
since      1988
says       With TZ="PCS5PCD,M3.2.0,M11.1.0", localtime() gives standard
           time (5 h west, tm_isdst 0) until the second Sunday of March
           at 02:00 standard time and from the first Sunday of November
           at 02:00 Daylight Saving Time, and Daylight Saving Time (4 h
           west, tm_isdst positive) between, checked one second either
           side of each change in 2021 and 2026 and at midsummer and
           midwinter.
note       No offset after dst: DST is one hour ahead; no time after a
           date: the change is at 02:00 (XBD 8.3).
test       t/002-dst-rule-m.c

assertion  XSH.localtime.003
anchor     functions/localtime.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap08.html#8.3/TZ
class      required
since      1988
says       With TZ="PCS5PCD4:30,J60/3,300/1:30", DST (4 h 30 min west)
           starts on 1 March at 03:00 standard time in both 2023 and the
           leap year 2024 (Jn does not count 29 February) and ends at
           01:30 DST on day 300 counted from 0 with 29 February counted
           (28 October 2023, 27 October 2024).
test       t/003-dst-rule-julian.c

assertion  XSH.localtime.004
anchor     functions/localtime.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap08.html#8.3/TZ
class      required
since      1988
says       With TZ="PCW-10PCX,M10.1.0,M4.1.0/3" (the end earlier in the
           year than the start), the year begins and ends in DST: 11 h
           east with tm_isdst positive in January and December, 10 h east
           with tm_isdst 0 in July, and the changes of 2021 (4 April
           03:00 DST, 3 October 02:00 standard time) fall where the rule
           puts them.
test       t/004-dst-rule-south.c

assertion  XSH.localtime.005
anchor     functions/localtime.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap08.html#8.3/TZ
class      required
says       A rule time may be negative or above 24 hours: with
           TZ="PCS5PCD,M3.2.0/-1,M11.1.0/26", DST starts on Saturday 13
           March 2021 at 23:00 standard time and ends on Monday 8 November
           2021 at 02:00 DST (checked one second either side).
test       t/005-rule-times.c

assertion  XSH.localtime.006
anchor     functions/localtime.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap08.html#8.3/TZ
class      required
says       With TZ="PCS5PCD,0/0,J365/25" DST is in effect all year (4 h
           west, tm_isdst positive): at midsummer, and every half hour
           from 03:00 to 07:00 UTC on 1 January 2021 and 2022, where the
           end of one year's DST meets the start of the next.
note       The all-year form XBD 8.3 itself describes, with our own
           names.
test       t/006-all-year-dst.c

assertion  XSH.localtime.007
anchor     functions/localtime.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       After tzset() with TZ="PCT3", TZ is changed to
           "PCE-5:30" without calling tzset(): localtime() then converts
           with the new offset, and tzname[0] is "PCE" afterwards.
test       t/007-sets-tz-info.c

assertion  XSH.localtime.008
anchor     functions/localtime.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/localtime.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       After tzset(), localtime_r() stores into *result the local
           time localtime() gives for the same value (standard time,
           DST, and both sides of a change under the rule of
           XSH.localtime.002) and returns result.
test       t/008-localtime-r.c

assertion  XSH.localtime.009
anchor     functions/localtime.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       After tzset() with TZ="PCA3", TZ is changed to
           "PCB-2PCC,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3" and localtime_r() is called:
           afterwards tzname, daylight and timezone either all still
           describe PCA3 (localtime_r() set none of them) or all describe
           the new value (it set all three).
note       The result's own offset is not checked: localtime_r() need
           not take a changed TZ into account (APPLICATION USAGE of
           tzset()).
test       t/009-r-tzname-rule.c

assertion  XSH.localtime.010
anchor     functions/localtime.html#ERRORS/EOVERFLOW
anchor     functions/localtime.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       localtime() of the largest time_t value, with TZ="PCT3",
           returns a null pointer and sets errno to EOVERFLOW.
note       UNRESOLVED where int is wide enough to hold that year.
test       t/010-eoverflow.c

assertion  XSH.localtime.011
anchor     functions/localtime.html#ERRORS/EOVERFLOW
anchor     functions/localtime.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       localtime_r() of the largest time_t value, with TZ="PCT3",
           returns a null pointer and sets errno to EOVERFLOW.
note       UNRESOLVED where int is wide enough to hold that year.
test       t/011-r-eoverflow.c

assertion  XSH.localtime.012
anchor     functions/localtime.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/time.h.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       With TZ="PCS5PCD,M3.2.0,M11.1.0", localtime() and
           localtime_r() set tm_gmtoff to -18000 and tm_zone to "PCS" in
           January, and tm_gmtoff to -14400 and tm_zone to "PCD" in July.
note       Names tm_gmtoff and tm_zone; a system whose <time.h> hides
           them under the strict build cannot compile the test.
test       t/012-gmtoff-zone.c
